.TH HU_SPAWN 3 "" "helios-unix" "Library functions"
.SH NAME
hu_spawn, hu_spawnp, hu_spawn_actions_init, hu_spawn_actions_destroy, hu_spawn_addclose, hu_spawn_adddup2, hu_spawn_addopen \- launch a native Helios task
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <helios/unix/spawn.h>

void hu_spawn_actions_init(struct hu_spawn_actions *actions);
void hu_spawn_actions_destroy(struct hu_spawn_actions *actions);
int hu_spawn_addclose(struct hu_spawn_actions *actions, int fd);
int hu_spawn_adddup2(struct hu_spawn_actions *actions, int from, int to);
int hu_spawn_addopen(struct hu_spawn_actions *actions, int fd,
                     const char *path, int flags);
int hu_spawn(pid_t *pid, const char *path,
             const struct hu_spawn_actions *actions,
             const struct hu_spawn_attr *attr,
             char *const argv[], char *const envp[]);
int hu_spawnp(pid_t *pid, const char *name,
              const struct hu_spawn_actions *actions,
              const struct hu_spawn_attr *attr,
              char *const argv[], char *const envp[]);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Launch a new task without copying the parent's address space.
hu_spawnp searches the caller's PATH if the name contains no slash.
NULL envp inherits the environment. Argument and environment arrays end with
a NULL pointer. A successful call writes a PID usable with waitpid and kill.
.PP
Initialize an action list before adding actions and destroy it afterwards,
including on error. addopen copies its pathname. Actions apply in order to
the child's descriptor description without changing the parent's descriptors.
There are at most 32 actions; descriptor numbers must be in 0..4095.
Opening or truncating a file can have effects even if later launch steps fail.
.PP
NULL actions means no descriptor actions. NULL attr selects defaults.
Otherwise zero-initialize struct hu_spawn_attr and set the desired fields:
.TP
placement
HU_SPAWN_DEFAULT uses normal task placement, including the session's Taskforce
Manager where available. HU_SPAWN_LOCAL selects this processor.
HU_SPAWN_PROCESSOR selects the processor named by processor.
.TP
processor
Processor object pathname, required for HU_SPAWN_PROCESSOR.
.TP
directory
Child working directory; NULL keeps the current directory.
.TP
closefrom
Close child descriptors at or above this number after actions; 0 disables
this step. FD_CLOEXEC descriptors are also excluded.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Launch and add-action functions return 0 or an error number such as EINVAL,
ENOMEM or ENOENT. Use strerror on that value; do not assume errno contains it.
The PID is valid only after a successful launch.
.SH EXAMPLE
Launch a command with only its standard descriptors, then wait for it.
.EX
#include <helios/unix/spawn.h>
#include <sys/wait.h>
#include <errno.h>

int run_command(char *const argv[], int *status)
{
    struct hu_spawn_attr attr = {0};
    pid_t pid, waited;
    int error;
    attr.closefrom = 3;
    error = hu_spawnp(&pid, argv[0], 0, &attr, argv, 0);
    if (error) return error;
    do { waited = waitpid(pid, status, 0); }
    while (waited < 0 && errno == EINTR);
    return waited < 0 ? errno : 0;
}
.EE
.SH NOTES
Use hu_channel for streams that must survive launching tasks on separate
processors. Descriptor inheritance does not provide Unix shared file-offset
or status-flag semantics. Do not perform concurrent spawn and close operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
hu_channel(3), hu_resolve(3), helios-unix(7)
